From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ae-automation-bot <ae-automation-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 08:48:37 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 140/159] [ae-patch] Size the session menus to their rows and
 give New Chat the same menu

The chat's session menu was a fixed 19rem and the harness row menu above it a
fixed 17.5rem, so the model names sat far from their shortcut digits, while the
Account, Effort and Previous models submenus each sized their own way and the
Account scope hint stretched its submenu to 334px. All of them now share
AE_MENU_WIDTH_CLASS (w-max, a 10rem floor, the viewport cap); the hint and the
error lines wrap under the rows instead of setting the width; the Previous
models chevron sits at the right edge like Account and Effort.

New Chat's Claude Code and Codex picker drew upstream's sectioned list (account
chips, inline effort, checks on the right). The chat's compact list moves into
AeCompactSessionChoices.tsx and New Chat renders it, with the Account submenu
and the digit shortcuts, for claude-native and codex-native without a sandbox
catalog. HarnessPickerEntry takes a configClassName so that submenu shares the
width rule. The New Chat suites open the Effort and Previous models submenus
before picking.
